exp="Long-acting nitrates lose effect with continuous use: <b>nitrate tolerance</b>. The fix is a <b>nitrate-free interval, usually overnight</b>, so tolerance can't build up. For a patch, remove it at night (worn ~12–14 h). Dr. Scully links this to the OMK 1 \"<b>Monday morning headache</b>\": munitions workers became tolerant during the work week, lost it over the weekend, and got headaches again on Monday.<br><br><b>Educational objective:</b> Nitrate tolerance develops with continuous exposure. Prevent it with a daily nitrate-free interval, usually overnight.",
wrong={1:"Higher continuous doses still cause tolerance and more headache and hypotension.",
2:"A continuous IV infusion causes tolerance too.",
3:"PDE5 inhibitors with nitrates cause refractory hypotension and are contraindicated.",
4:"Continuous exposure is the cause of tolerance."},
